{"repositoryId":1380656309,"availability":"available","full":"Yaser-Alharbi/Kidney-Blood-Vessel-Segmentation","name":"Kidney-Blood-Vessel-Segmentation","description":"U-Net blood-vessel segmentation in kidney histology: a study of stain augmentation and normalisation (HuBMAP).","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-21T23:48:47Z","updated":"2026-10-14T11:25:36Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://yaser-alharbi.github.io/Kidney-Blood-Vessel-Segmentation/","topics":["computational-pathology","computer-vision","data-augmentation","deep-learning","histopathology","hubmap","kaggle","medical-imaging","pytorch","semantic-segmentation","stain-normalization","streamlit","unet"],"demo":"https://yaser-alharbi.github.io/Kidney-Blood-Vessel-Segmentation/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:54.310Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:54.310Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:54.310Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T02:59:54.310Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["U-Net with a ResNet-34 encoder, trained under four stain-augmentation strategies and evaluated for robustness to inter-laboratory stain variation.","Pathology labs stain tissue slightly differently, and a segmentation model trained on one lab's colours can lose accuracy on another's. This project trains the same U-Net (ResNet-34 encoder, ImageNet weights) four ways, changing only how stain colour is handled, and repeats each recipe with 20 random seeds (80 runs). Data: the HuBMAP Hacking the Human Vasculature kidney tiles, with the split made by whole-slide image so no slide appears in more than one split."],"features":["Story site (methods, every number explained):","Live lab (run the models in your browser):"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Yaser-Alharbi/Kidney-Blood-Vessel-Segmentation/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c84c6d2a3fd030065d717a39145470551138116e4f430f297b0d76